1
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:09,570
Universities offer students a wealth of resources, yet many students use only a small part of them.
大学为学生提供了丰富的资源，然而许多学生只利用了其中的一小部分。

2
00:00:10,370 --> 00:00:17,170
In my opinion, making the best use of on-campus resources is one of the keys to academic development.
在我看来，充分利用校内资源是学业发展的关键之一。

3
00:00:17,970 --> 00:00:20,640
The library is the most obvious place to start.
图书馆是最显而易见的起点。

4
00:00:21,440 --> 00:00:30,360
Apart from borrowing books, students can search its online databases for up-to-date research and attend its training sessions on finding information.
除了借书以外，学生还可以检索图书馆的在线数据库，获取最新的研究成果，并参加关于如何查找信息的培训课程。

5
00:00:31,160 --> 00:00:33,480
Teachers are another valuable resource.
教师是另一种宝贵的资源。

6
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:42,900
Instead of meeting professors only in class, students should visit them during office hours to discuss questions and seek advice on further study.
学生不应只在课堂上见到教授，而应在他们的答疑时间去拜访，讨论问题，并就进一步深造征求建议。

7
00:00:43,700 --> 00:00:51,970
In addition, laboratories, academic lectures and student research groups provide opportunities to apply knowledge and explore new fields.
此外，实验室、学术讲座和学生研究小组也为学生提供了运用知识和探索新领域的机会。

8
00:00:52,770 --> 00:00:57,980
To get the most out of these resources, students need to plan ahead and take the initiative.
要充分利用这些资源，学生需要提前规划，积极主动。

9
00:00:58,780 --> 00:01:05,230
For example, they can check the lecture schedule every week and set aside regular time for the library.
例如，他们可以每周查看讲座安排，并留出固定的时间去图书馆。

10
00:01:06,030 --> 00:01:15,410
Those who actively explore what their university offers will not only improve their academic performance but also develop the ability to learn independently.
那些积极发掘学校资源的学生，不仅能提高学习成绩，还能培养自主学习的能力。
